        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "The living ocean"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Over 70 percent of the Earth is ocean. It gives us food, weather, trade routes and also dangers like tsunamis and cyclones."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "currents",
          "maritime zones",
          "ocean relief",
          "protection",
          "resources",
          "tsunami and cyclone warnings",
          "water movements",
          "waves and tides"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "The ocean floor has relief: the continental shelf, the continental slope, the deep sea plain and trenches.\nOcean water is always in motion as waves, tides and currents.\nWaves are caused by wind. Tides are the rise and fall of sea level due to the pull of the Moon and the Sun.\nOcean currents are streams of water moving in definite directions. They affect climate and fishing.\nA country's maritime zones include the territorial sea up to 12 nautical miles and the exclusive economic zone up to 200 nautical miles.\nOceans give fish, oil, gas, minerals, salt and energy, so they must be used sustainably.\nTsunamis are huge waves caused by undersea earthquakes. Early warning systems and cyclone alerts save lives.\nReducing plastic and overfishing protects ocean life."
        }
